For Contributions, the Licensor may transfer and sublicense this patent license through multiple levels to support the exploitation and relicensing authorized by Section 9. Coverage does not extend to claims infringed only because of later additions or combinations beyond the contributed implementation and its combination with the Work as submitted. These grants continue for the relevant patents' duration and are irrevocable except for termination expressly provided by this License or required by law.

If a beneficiary of a patent grant under this Section initiates or directs patent litigation, including an infringement counterclaim or cross-claim, alleging that the Work or an incorporated Contribution infringes a patent it owns or controls, all patent permissions granted to that claimant under this License for that Work terminate when the claim is filed. Defending a claim without asserting such infringement does not trigger termination.

Patent retaliation does not terminate unrelated parties' rights. Restoration requires written consent from the relevant patent grantor and is not guaranteed by Section 13. No additional patent rights are implied, and copyright permissions do not supply missing patent rights.

