13. Termination and Cure

Your permissions terminate automatically upon a material breach of this License, subject to mandatory law.

For a first, unintentional, curable material breach, permissions are automatically reinstated when You stop the breach and complete reasonably practicable corrective measures for consequences within Your control, provided this occurs before notice or within 30 days after receiving written notice describing the breach with reasonable specificity.

Intentional unauthorized Commercialization, deliberate operation of an unauthorized fork or Project-as-a-Service, and repeated material breaches after prior notice do not receive automatic reinstatement. The Licensor may nevertheless reinstate permissions by Written Permission. Obtaining another copy does not itself reinstate terminated permissions. Patent retaliation is governed separately by Section 10.

Upon termination, stop exercising the terminated permissions and cease unauthorized distribution and services. You may retain non-operational copies required for legal compliance or evidence, and inaccessible routine backups until ordinarily overwritten, but may not use that retention to continue prohibited activity.

Reinstatement does not automatically waive claims arising before cure. Termination does not terminate compliant recipients' direct licenses or grants You have made under Sections 9 and 10, except as expressly stated there. Ownership provisions, accrued claims, disclaimers, liability limitations, and provisions necessary to interpret surviving rights remain effective.

